    "blocking_factual_correction": null,
    "qualifications": [
      "The inactive 255 optimization uses physical 8-bit selector fields and SeriesPack byte identity transfers, even when logical F is less than 8. It is not permission to store 255 through a packed narrower logical format.",
      "Clear/reuse must restore every previously live selector to the inactive encoding before count-free lookup. Clone/rebuild/migration and refusal must preserve the same invariant; erase-last gains a real store and damage event.",
      "The proposed last 8-byte row transfer at offset 120 fits a 128-byte owner unit, but its permission must still be admitted from that owner. A semantic exact 5-byte row or field view alone cannot authorize it.",
      "The proposal already charges mutation and initialization costs and preserves count fallback for real fingerprint 255, independent descendant accounting, static capacity masks and wider-read permission."
    ]
  }
}
